      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "(Gonna lump earmuff mode into this comment as well since it seems related)\n\nI feel like it's pretty common for audience members to want to cull and muffle the audience without affecting the presenters, and it's unfortunate that the vrc client only has distance-based options with no available exceptions for unmuffling/unculling specific people, or exceptions for udon when people are detected on stage.\n\nOn the other hand, as a player it does make sense for my distance-based culling (and earmuff) settings to be respected above all else. If I'm not in the theater area of a world, I probably don't want udon to give the MC's microhone global voice distance that bypasses my earmuff settings, or have the world make the DJ's flashy/unoptimized avatar render when I'm nowhere nearby.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
